      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level, the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for acute pain or inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (1,200\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual range\n- **1,600 mg per day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf the dose is intentional, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and I can enter it with a note documenting that. I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
